message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PyNTLP: Adaptive Quantile Flexibility (AQF) — code and artifacts"
abstract: >-
  PyNTLP (Python for Network Tariff to Load Profile) estimates how electricity
  network tariff designs could change customer load profiles. It contains the
  Spark-native pyntlp package implementing the Solar Sharer Offer
  tariff-to-load-profile model, and standalone research code for Adaptive
  Quantile Flexibility (AQF), a method for estimating the flexible component of
  aggregate metered demand by computing the bias-minimising quantile from the
  estimated frequency and size of flexible events rather than hand-picking it.
type: software
